    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«にあたって» places an important action or decision on a specific occasion.",
     "texto": [
      "It's typical of formal contexts, such as an opening, a move or the start of a project. For an everyday moment, 〜とき is usually more natural.",
      "新しい 図書館 を 開く に あたって、市民 の 意見 を 参考 に しました。 (When opening the new library, the citizens' opinions were taken into account.)",
      "計画 を 始める に あたって、安全 面 を もう一度 確認 しました。 (When starting the plan, the safety aspects were checked once more.)"
     ],
